  "description": "Revised front boundary treatment comprising a 1.2m high visually permeable slatted larch fence, integrated timber bin store and associated front garden landscaping.\n\nThe proposal forms part of a wider landscape-led enhancement to the front garden, replacing the former concrete hardstanding with permeable gravel surfacing, increased planting and an integrated timber bin store to improve biodiversity, drainage and the appearance of the frontage.\n\nThe boundary treatment is limited to the section adjoining the neighbouring rear gardens and does not extend across the full frontage, maintaining an open entrance, clear sightlines and views of the house from the public highway. Its visually permeable design and natural larch finish create a lightweight appearance that complements the streetscape while providing an appropriate degree of enclosure for integrated refuse storage.",
